From 75a3aa2a5cd330de25fa23cd7b23558641c686f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Burke Cates <burke.cates@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:35:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] NOT-FOR-UPSTREAM: ASoC: soc-core: leave trigger-muted DAIs muted on
 system resume

soc_resume_deferred() unmutes every active playback DAI. For a DAI with
mute_unmute_on_trigger that is too early: the PCM is still suspended
until user space resumes or restarts it, and the RESUME or START trigger
unmutes the DAI then anyway (snd_soc_pcm_dai_trigger()).

On the ASUS Zenbook A16 (Glymur, four WSA8845 on two SoundWire buses)
the WSA884x mute_stream() sets GLOBAL_PA_EN, so every s2idle resume with
the speaker PCM open turned the amplifiers on about two seconds before
the stream ran again, while the SoundWire buses were still coming out of
clock stop: an audible burst on each resume, recorded with an external
microphone. With the PCM closed there was none.

Skip the unmute for such DAIs; the suspend-time mute is unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (claude-opus-5-5)
---
Not-for-upstream: local workaround for one laptop, not reviewed for
  submission; use only for local testing.

 sound/soc/soc-core.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/soc-core.c b/sound/soc/soc-core.c
index b9c70268d49f..925fbf795bc6 100644
--- a/sound/soc/soc-core.c
+++ b/sound/soc/soc-core.c
@@ -631,8 +631,17 @@ static void soc_playback_digital_mute(struct snd_soc_card *card, int mute)
 			continue;
 
 		for_each_rtd_dais(rtd, i, dai) {
-			if (snd_soc_dai_stream_active(dai, playback))
-				snd_soc_dai_digital_mute(dai, mute, playback);
+			if (!snd_soc_dai_stream_active(dai, playback))
+				continue;
+			/*
+			 * A DAI that is unmuted at trigger time gets unmuted
+			 * by the RESUME or START trigger, once the stream
+			 * runs again. Unmuting it here, while the stream is
+			 * still suspended, turns the output on with no data.
+			 */
+			if (!mute && snd_soc_dai_mute_is_ctrled_at_trigger(dai))
+				continue;
+			snd_soc_dai_digital_mute(dai, mute, playback);
 		}
 	}
 }
